content:
Dispatch and completion of a Marlowe & Finch Home Delivery are recorded by the delivery team: the booking goes out for delivery when the truck leaves, and is delivered when the team completes the delivery and the customer signs or confirms.

## What the team does at the address

The team, according to the booking's service level:

- calls the level's call-ahead time, in minutes, before arrival;
- places items at the level's placement;
- removes packaging where the level includes packaging removal;
- assembles within the level's included assembly time where the level includes assembly;
- hauls away where haul-away is included or bought;
- uses floor protection where the level includes floor protection;
- inspects items with the customer where the level includes inspection at delivery;
- collects a signature where the level requires one.

Haul-away is part of the service where the level includes haul-away. A two-person team is sent where the level provides one. Contactless drop-off is offered only where the level offers a contactless option, and then no signature or inspection is taken.

## Contactless drop-off and the hand-over

| Level offers contactless drop-off | Customer chooses contactless drop-off | Signature and inspection |
|---|---|---|
| Yes | Yes | No signature or inspection is taken |
| Yes | No | Taken where the level requires a signature or includes inspection |
| No | Not offered | Taken where the level requires a signature or includes inspection |

## Damage

**Damage to the home** is claimed as a delivery claim within the level's reporting period, in hours, after delivery, and is compensated by the claims team up to the level's maximum compensation for damage to the home, within the level's claim resolution period in business days.

**Damaged or missing merchandise** is handled under the Merchandise Purchases order return rules for damage in transit.

*Hypothetical claim, reporting period of 48 hours, delivery completed Monday at 11:00:* a report on Wednesday at 10:00, 47 hours after delivery, is within the period; a report on Wednesday at 12:00, 49 hours after, is not.

*Hypothetical compensation, maximum compensation of $1,000.00:* assessed damage of $640.00 is compensated up to $640.00; assessed damage of $1,600.00 is compensated up to $1,000.00.
